{"1-3":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"jeduthun-h3038g","name":"Jeduthun","kind":"person","brief":"A Singer","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3956","lemma":"לָשׁוֹן","tr":"la·shon","gloss":"tongue","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":117},{"base":"H1901","lemma":"הָגִיג","tr":"ha·gig","gloss":"meditation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H8104","lemma":"שָׁמַר","tr":"sha·mar","gloss":"to keep: obey","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":469},{"base":"H1747","lemma":"דּוּמִיָּה","tr":"du·miy·yah","gloss":"silence","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H3511","lemma":"כְּאֵב","tr":"ke·ev","gloss":"pain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H0481","lemma":"אָלַם","tr":"a·lam","gloss":"be dumb","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H5916","lemma":"עָכַר","tr":"a·khar","gloss":"to trouble","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H2814","lemma":"חָשָׁה","tr":"cha·shah","gloss":"be silent","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H2552","lemma":"חָמַם","tr":"cha·mam","gloss":"to warm","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H1197","lemma":"בָּעַר","tr":"ba·ar","gloss":"to burn: burn","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":94}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":30,"source":"both","text":"He who guards his mouth and tongue keeps his soul from distress.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":141,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"Set a guard, O LORD, over my mouth; keep watch at the door of my lips.","from":1},{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"If anyone considers himself religious and yet does not bridle his tongue, he deceives his heart and his religion is worthless.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"How can a young man keep his way pure? By guarding it according to Your word.","from":1},{"book":"MIC","chapter":7,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"Do not rely on a friend; do not trust in a companion. Seal the doors of your mouth from her who lies in your arms.","from":1},{"book":"MIC","chapter":7,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"For a son dishonors his father, a daughter rises against her mother, and a daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law. A manʼs enemies are the members of his own household.","from":1},{"book":"JAS","chapter":3,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"We all stumble in many ways. If anyone is never at fault in what he says, he is a perfect man, able to control his whole body.","from":1},{"book":"JAS","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"but no man can tame the tongue. It is a restless evil, full of deadly poison.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"4-6":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0389","lemma":"אַךְ","tr":"akh","gloss":"surely","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":161},{"base":"H1892","lemma":"הֶ֫בֶל","tr":"he·vel","gloss":"vanity","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":73},{"base":"H3045","lemma":"יָדַע","tr":"ya·da","gloss":"to know","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":945},{"base":"H2310","lemma":"חָדֵל","tr":"cha·del","gloss":"rejected","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H2947","lemma":"טֶ֫פַח","tr":"te·phach","gloss":"handbreadth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H2465","lemma":"חֶ֫לֶד","tr":"che·led","gloss":"lifetime","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H6651","lemma":"צָבַר","tr":"tsa·var","gloss":"to heap","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H4100","lemma":"מָה","tr":"mah","gloss":"what?","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":752},{"base":"H6754","lemma":"צֶ֫לֶם","tr":"tse·lem","gloss":"image","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H1993","lemma":"הָמָה","tr":"ha·mah","gloss":"to roar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":34}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":90,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"So teach us to number our days, that we may present a heart of wisdom.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":103,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"For He knows our frame; He is mindful that we are dust.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":144,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Man is like a breath; his days are like a passing shadow.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":89,"verse":47,"verseEnd":47,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Remember the briefness of my lifespan! For what futility You have created all men!","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":62,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Lowborn men are but a vapor; the exalted are but a lie. Weighed on the scale, they go up; together they are but a vapor.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":90,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"For all our days decline in Your fury; we finish our years with a sigh.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":90,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"The length of our days is seventy years— or eighty if we are strong— yet their pride is but labor and sorrow, for they quickly pass, and we fly away.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":84,"verseEnd":84,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"How many days must Your servant wait? When will You execute judgment on my persecutors?","from":4}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"7-11":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H4529","lemma":"מָסָה","tr":"ma·sah","gloss":"to liquefy","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H8431","lemma":"תּוֹחֶ֫לֶת","tr":"to·che·let","gloss":"hope","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H0481","lemma":"אָלַם","tr":"a·lam","gloss":"be dumb","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H6211","lemma":"עָשׁ","tr":"ash","gloss":"moth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H5036","lemma":"נָבָל","tr":"na·val","gloss":"foolish","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H2530","lemma":"חָמַד","tr":"cha·mad","gloss":"to desire","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":25},{"base":"H8433","lemma":"תּוֹכֵחָה","tr":"to·khe·chah","gloss":"rebuke","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":28},{"base":"H3256","lemma":"יָסַר","tr":"ya·sar","gloss":"to discipline","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":43},{"base":"H6960","lemma":"קָוָה","tr":"qa·vah","gloss":"to await","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":49},{"base":"H1892","lemma":"הֶ֫בֶל","tr":"he·vel","gloss":"vanity","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":73}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ROM","chapter":15,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"Now may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace as you believe in Him, so that you may overflow with hope by the power of the Holy Spirit.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":38,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"I wait for You, O LORD; You will answer, O Lord my God.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":81,"verseEnd":81,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"My soul faints for Your salvation; I wait for Your word.","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"I await Your salvation, O Lord.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":166,"verseEnd":166,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"I wait for Your salvation, O LORD, and I carry out Your commandments.","from":7},{"book":"JOB","chapter":13,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Though He slay me, I will hope in Him. I will still defend my ways to His face.","from":7},{"book":"JOB","chapter":9,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Let Him remove His rod from me, so that His terror will no longer frighten me.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":130,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"I wait for the LORD; my soul does wait, and in His word I put my hope.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"12-13":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H1082","lemma":"בָּלַג","tr":"ba·lag","gloss":"be cheerful","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7775","lemma":"שַׁוְעָה","tr":"shav·ah","gloss":"cry","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H8453","lemma":"תּוֹשָׁב","tr":"to·shav","gloss":"sojourner","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H8159","lemma":"שָׁעָה","tr":"sha·ah","gloss":"to gaze","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H1832","lemma":"דִּמְעָה","tr":"dim·ah","gloss":"tears","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23},{"base":"H0238","lemma":"אָזַן","tr":"a·zan","gloss":"to listen","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":41},{"base":"H2962","lemma":"טֶ֫רֶם","tr":"te·rem","gloss":"before","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":56},{"base":"H2790","lemma":"חָרַשׁ","tr":"cha·rash","gloss":"to plow","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":74},{"base":"H8605","lemma":"תְּפִלָּה","tr":"te·phil·lah","gloss":"prayer","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":77},{"base":"H1616","lemma":"גֵּר","tr":"ger","gloss":"sojourner","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":92}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1PE","chapter":2,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Beloved, I urge you, as foreigners and exiles, to abstain from the desires of the flesh, which war against your soul.","from":12},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"All these people died in faith, without having received the things they were promised. However, they saw them and welcomed them from afar. And they acknowledged that they were strangers and exiles on the earth.","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":47,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"“My travels have lasted 130 years,” Jacob replied. “My years have been few and hard, and they have not matched the years of the travels of my fathers.”","from":12},{"book":"LEV","chapter":25,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The land must not be sold permanently, because it is Mine, and you are but foreigners and residents with Me.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"I am a stranger on the earth; do not hide Your commandments from me.","from":12},{"book":"2KI","chapter":20,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"“Go back and tell Hezekiah the leader of My people that this is what the LORD, the God of your father David, says: ‘I have heard your prayer; I have seen your tears. I will surely heal you. On the third day from now you will go up to the house of the LORD.","from":12},{"book":"1CH","chapter":29,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"For we are foreigners and strangers in Your presence, as were all our forefathers. Our days on earth are like a shadow, without hope.","from":12},{"book":"PSA","chapter":56,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"You have taken account of my wanderings. Put my tears in Your bottle— are they not in Your book?","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}